    "result_text": "All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`). The redesign is complete. Here's what I changed and why:\n\n## Summary\n\n**New identity format** \u2014 `customerCode` is now `<REGION>-<HASH8>` (e.g. `NSW-16E6609E`), with the per-city sequence dropped entirely.\n\n### Core changes\n- **`OwnerCustomerCodes`** (rewritten) \u2014 the single home for the format. Builds `<REGION>-<HASH8>` where REGION comes from the postcode and HASH8 is the first 8 upper-case hex chars of SHA-256 over `normalizedTelephone + lastName`. The telephone is put through the existing `OwnerTelephones.toE164` so the hash always sees the normalized form.\n- **`AssignOwnerCustomerCode`** \u2014 no longer scans the repository or computes a sequence; it just asks `OwnerCustomerCodes.forOwner(owner)`. Dropped the now-unused `OwnerRepository` dependency.\n- **`Locality`** \u2014 added `forPostcode(postcode)` (postcode \u2192 region, else `UNKNOWN`) and removed the now-unused `forCityAndPostcode`. This is the *single* region derivation shared by the customer code and the locality field, so an owner's locality and the REGION segment of their code always agree.\n- **`OwnerMapper.locality(...)`** \u2014 moved onto that same region-and-hash identity via `Locality.forPostcode(owner.getPostcode())`.\n\n### Values built from the customer code\n- **Membership number** (`<customerCode>-M<YY>`) and **Luhn check digit** already derive from `customerCode` in the mapper, so they follow the new identity automatically \u2014 I only refreshed the stale `LON-SMI-0007` javadoc example.\n- **Audit record** logs `owner.getCustomerCode()`, so it now emits the new identity with no code change (verified in the test log: `customerCode=NSW-16E6609E`).\n\n### Reuse / hygiene\n- Extracted the duplicated SHA-256-to-hex logic into **`util/Sha256.hex(...)`**, now used by both `OwnerHouseholds` and `OwnerCustomerCodes` instead of copying it.\n- Updated the stale `RequireCityCapacity` comment (it referenced the removed sequence counting) and the three affected `openapi.yml` descriptions/examples (`customerCode`, `membershipNumber`, `locality`).\n\n`./mvnw test` \u2192 **BUILD SUCCESS**, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.",
